<title>USA: Enron buys rights to build power plants.</title>
<headline>Enron buys rights to build power plants.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Enron Ventures Corp said Friday it acquired  National Energy Production Corp's rights to build three power plants  from Zurn Industries Inc for undisclosed terms.</p>
<p>The Enron Corp subsidiary acquired National Energy's contracts to  construct the 160 megawatt Kabirwala power project in Pakistan, two  120 megawatt cogeneration projects at the Rojana and Saha Pathana  industrial parks in Thailand, and a 335 megawatt cogeneration plant  at a refinery site in Sweeny, Texas.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
